    {
      "id": "claim_cb8aa1ad51a3455fa0f96ae56e04424d",
      "statement": "FeedPollingScheduler.pollAndAdjust re-reads the feed's current errorCount from the database after every poll and recomputes the effective interval via computeEffectiveInterval: when errorCount >= backoffThreshold (default 5) the interval is pollIntervalMinutes * 2^(errorCount/backoffThreshold), with the exponent capped at 30 and the multiplication done in long arithmetic to avoid overflowing into a negative Duration, then clamped to maxIntervalMinutes (default 1440); otherwise the interval is just pollIntervalMinutes. If the desired interval differs from the currently scheduled one, the task is cancelled and rescheduled to start one full interval from now.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/scheduler/FeedPollingScheduler.java#L79-L120",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:20df92db0bc1122b868d22265b3cca6c41018f51b21c6c3dc0bd6e9f1a879d9a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_67429ce8f8ac470a9af27b9f4d0ee3ba",
      "statement": "The interval re-evaluation step inside pollAndAdjust is wrapped in its own try/catch that logs a warning and keeps the current schedule on failure, so a transient error during re-evaluation (e.g. a DB blip) cannot silently unschedule a feed; FeedPollingScheduler also self-cancels a feed's task if pollFeed throws NotFoundException, indicating the feed was deleted mid-flight.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/scheduler/FeedPollingScheduler.java#L79-L103",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:02752606030ef7103fe0f2c199c9826abf50d96ed42d43a6b706b9075b983f8c:"
        }
      ]
    },
