      "id": "claim_4d58ddbc6497464bb2fe4303f8cd649a",
      "statement": "GET /api/articles/{id}/extracted-content (ArticleController.extractedContent) delegates to ArticleExtractionService.extract, which returns the cached article.extracted_content when present (via ArticleRepository.findExtractedContent, no network call), and otherwise re-fetches the article's original page through FeedFetcher.fetch(url) (the same fetch path used by subscribe/poll, so the SSRF guard and size cap both apply), extracts readable content with Readability4J's Readability4J(url, html).parse(), caches the resulting HTML via ArticleRepository.saveExtractedContent, and throws FeedParseException (422) if nothing readable is extracted, NotFoundException (404) if the article doesn't exist, or IllegalArgumentException (400) if the article has no URL.",
