    {
      "id": "claim_0cbc6197d49f448e9d906a67f2f59d26",
      "statement": "FeedFetcher is the single outbound fetch path for feed and article-page content: every fetch first calls FeedUrlValidator.validate(url), which requires an http/https scheme and rejects hosts resolving to loopback, link-local, RFC1918/site-local, any-local, multicast, carrier-grade-NAT (100.64.0.0/10), limited-broadcast, or IPv6 unique-local (fc00::/7) addresses, throwing IllegalArgumentException (mapped to 400) on violation; this SSRF guard applies equally to subscribe, polling, and ArticleExtractionService's re-fetch of an article's original page since all three call FeedFetcher.fetch.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/service/FeedFetcher.java#L37-L80",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1c4b35af54b3420264f32ddc8a0f1225db0679e6e070e8fcad57242b20cb4919:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/service/FeedUrlValidator.java#L55-L135",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d75e12636d4a7372f44eaf895da7fadebc9fcc8d3034b3b4f0c604b915bb1c22:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_71abcff9399947ae958d27fc235bec61",
      "statement": "FeedUrlValidator documents two accepted limitations for the single-user LAN deployment: it does not defend against DNS rebinding/TOCTOU between validation and the actual RestClient connection (since RestClient re-resolves the host), and it does not re-validate redirects per hop, so a permitted URL could redirect to a blocked address.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/main/java/org/bartram/myfeeder/service/FeedUrlValidator.java#L11-L27",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3f1782c78a25e4059be13d2718977111b5db15687ee393dd7ff454a408d05409:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_57674f33534240369167a99a3c9e0ac3",
      "statement": "FeedFetcher bounds every response body read to DEFAULT_MAX_FEED_BYTES (10 MiB) via response.getBody().readNBytes(maxFeedBytes + 1), throwing FeedFetchException (mapped to 422) if the body exceeds that cap, which bounds heap usage against an unbounded or malicious response.",
